From: =?UTF-8?q?Petr=20=C5=A0tetiar?= <petr.stetiar@prplfoundation.org>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 10:35:42 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ApMgt: keep default TTLM in link-ID space
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

An empty AdvertisedLinkMapFrequencyBands selects all available MLD
links. The validator already builds their bitmap from each active,
enabled link's radio band and actual link ID.

It then substitutes that link bitmap for a frequency-band mask and
converts it a second time. Link IDs do not identify bands: after link
remove/re-add they can be 3, 4 and 6 instead of 0, 1 and 2. Their bitmap
is then interpreted as bands, yielding a partial or empty selection. An
empty result returns before the backend call and datamodel mirror,
leaving an earlier advertised mapping in place when clearing it.

Return the already converted all-links bitmap for an empty band
selection. Keep the existing band-to-actual-link-ID conversion for
explicit selections. A successful clear now reaches the backend and
mirrors the empty band string, while backend failures preserve the last
applied value as for explicit mappings.

Signed-off-by: Petr Štetiar <petr.stetiar@prplfoundation.org>
---
 src/ApMgt/wld_apMld_tidLinkMap.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/ApMgt/wld_apMld_tidLinkMap.c b/src/ApMgt/wld_apMld_tidLinkMap.c
index 2c4fdc910fb0..390b9f5321bc 100644
--- a/src/ApMgt/wld_apMld_tidLinkMap.c
+++ b/src/ApMgt/wld_apMld_tidLinkMap.c
@@ -186,7 +186,7 @@ static wld_tidLinkMap_m s_getValidTidLinkMap(wld_mld_t* pMld) {
 
     swl_freqBand_m advertisedLinkMap = pMld->tidLinkMapConfig.advertisedLinkMapFreqBands;
     if(advertisedLinkMap == 0) {
-        advertisedLinkMap = availableLinks;
+        return availableLinks;
     }
 
     wld_tidLinkMap_m newBitMap = s_getLinksBitMapFromFreqBandMask(pMld, advertisedLinkMap);
